sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User
    participant A as AI Agent / MCP Client
    participant R as Secured MCP Registry
    participant G as SecureMCP Safety Pillars
    participant M as Approved MCP Service

    U->>A: 1. Ask the AI application to complete a task
    A->>A: 2. Identify the MCP capability needed
    A->>R: 3. Sign in and search approved services
    R->>G: 4. Check identity, trust, policy and permission
    G-->>R: 5. Return the access decision
    R-->>A: 6. Provide an approved service configuration
    A->>M: 7. Request the MCP capability
    M->>G: 8. Apply safety rules during use
    G->>G: 9. Reflexive Core checks behaviour and risk

    alt Normal behaviour
        G-->>M: 10A. Allow the action to continue
        M-->>A: 11A. Return the result
        A-->>U: 12A. Complete the user's task
    else Elevated risk
        G-->>A: 10B. Request approval or return a limited response
    else Critical risk
        G-->>M: 10C. Stop the action
        G->>R: 11C. Recommend suspension or revocation
        R-->>A: 12C. Disable the affected connection
    end

    G->>G: 13. Record provenance, audit and alerts
